13
00:00:36.885 --> 00:00:48.341
What you get: a reference platform that combines an online travel agency for hotels (like Booking.com, MakeMyTrip or Agoda) with a homestay marketplace (like Airbnb).

14
00:00:48.621 --> 00:01:06.413
It covers: supply onboarding: hotels via channel managers, and hosts listing homes;. the availability calendar and rate plans (room types, meal plans, refundable and non-refundable rates);. search by city, area or map, with dates and guests, at millions of searches an hour;.

15
00:01:07.763 --> 00:01:26.045
ranking and personalisation;. dynamic pricing and host price suggestions;. booking with holds and payments (pay now, pay at hotel, part-pay);. overbooking and channel sync problems;. cancellations and refunds, reviews and trust, host payouts, guest, host messaging, and fraud.

16
00:01:27.395 --> 00:01:43.865
It also explains the algorithms: calendar representation and date-range availability, geo search, learning-to-rank and embeddings, price elasticity and revenue management, overbooking control, review integrity, fraud detection and duplicate-listing detection.

17
00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:46.811
It ends with the data platform and tech stack.

