186
00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:57.155
Latency at a high look-to-book ratio.

187
00:10:57.435 --> 00:10:58.353
Booking path.

188
00:10:58.633 --> 00:10:59.465
Choice:

189
00:10:59.745 --> 00:11:07.638
Exact availability check and hold on the ARI store (or a live check with the hotel), then payment, then confirmation.

190
00:11:07.918 --> 00:11:08.601
Why:

191
00:11:08.881 --> 00:11:10.161
Correctness at booking.

192
00:11:10.441 --> 00:11:11.657
Truth for hotels.

193
00:11:11.937 --> 00:11:12.769
Choice:

194
00:11:13.049 --> 00:11:15.011
The channel manager or PMS.

195
00:11:15.291 --> 00:11:17.659
The OTA keeps a synchronised copy.

196
00:11:17.939 --> 00:11:18.622
Why:

197
00:11:18.902 --> 00:11:20.822
Many channels sell the same rooms.

198
00:11:22.172 --> 00:11:23.495
Truth for homestays.

199
00:11:23.775 --> 00:11:24.607
Choice:

200
00:11:24.887 --> 00:11:28.129
The platform calendar, with iCal import and export.

201
00:11:28.409 --> 00:11:29.092
Why:

202
00:11:29.372 --> 00:11:31.505
Single unit, so no double booking.

203
00:11:31.785 --> 00:11:32.617
Ranking.

204
00:11:32.897 --> 00:11:33.729
Choice:

205
00:11:34.009 --> 00:11:37.209
ML learning-to-rank on conversion, with business rules.

206
00:11:37.489 --> 00:11:38.172
Why:

207
00:11:38.452 --> 00:11:40.308
Revenue and guest satisfaction.

208
00:11:40.588 --> 00:11:41.441
Payments.

209
00:11:41.721 --> 00:11:42.553
Choice:

210
00:11:42.833 --> 00:11:49.916
Merchant model (OTA collects) plus agency model (pay at hotel), and escrow-like timing for homestays.

211
00:11:50.196 --> 00:11:50.879
Why:

212
00:11:51.159 --> 00:11:52.588
Flexibility, trust.

213
00:11:53.938 --> 00:11:54.855
Part 4.

214
00:11:55.135 --> 00:11:57.013
How It Works, Journeys End to End.

215
00:11:58.263 --> 00:12:01.505
Journey 1: a hotel updates prices and inventory.

216
00:12:01.785 --> 00:12:02.916
The hotel side.

217
00:12:03.196 --> 00:12:10.044
The revenue manager at a Goa resort raises prices for the New Year week in their PMS or channel manager.

218
00:12:10.324 --> 00:12:14.249
The channel manager pushes the update to every connected OTA.

219
00:12:14.529 --> 00:12:31.041
The message is an ARI update in OTA standard messages (for example, OTAHotelRateAmountNotifRQ, OTAHotelAvailNotifRQ; publicly documented OpenTravel schemas; VERIFY specific partner APIs).

220
00:12:31.321 --> 00:12:42.948
Example: room type Deluxe Sea View, rate plan Breakfast included, refundable, dates 28 Dec, 2 Jan, rate 18,000, rupeesmin stay 3 nights, 4 rooms available.

221
00:12:44.298 --> 00:12:45.642
Connectivity gateway.

222
00:12:45.922 --> 00:12:47.415
Authenticates the partner.

223
00:12:47.695 --> 00:12:52.303
Validates the message: known property and room mapping, sane dates and amounts.

224
00:12:52.583 --> 00:12:53.885
Acknowledges quickly.

225
00:12:54.165 --> 00:13:00.095
Writes the update to a Kafka topic per property partition, so updates for one property stay in order.

226
00:13:00.375 --> 00:13:01.634
ARI service.

227
00:13:02.984 --> 00:13:08.787
Consumes the update and applies the range update to the ARI store (§6.1).

228
00:13:09.067 --> 00:13:15.851
Records the update source and timestamp, and keeps the last update per cell to resolve out-of-order messages.

229
00:13:16.131 --> 00:13:17.453
Search cache refresh.

230
00:13:17.733 --> 00:13:20.421
The change emits AriChanged(property, dates).

231
00:13:20.701 --> 00:13:31.731
The availability and price cache recomputes summaries for that property, such as the cheapest available price per night per occupancy and a flag for whether min-stay rules allow a stay.

232
00:13:33.081 --> 00:13:35.769
The update reaches the search nodes within seconds.

233
00:13:36.049 --> 00:13:36.923
Monitoring.

234
00:13:37.203 --> 00:13:40.681
Partners with high error rates or mapping problems are flagged.

235
00:13:40.961 --> 00:13:47.361
Stale properties (no updates for a long time) are shown carefully or re-synced through a full refresh request.

236
00:13:48.711 --> 00:13:51.057
Journey 2: searching for a stay in Goa.

237
00:13:51.337 --> 00:13:52.105
Query.

238
00:13:52.385 --> 00:13:57.015
Anita searches North Goa, 29 Dec, 1 Jan, 2 adults in the app.

239
00:13:57.295 --> 00:14:00.772
Autocomplete resolves North Goa to a region polygon.

240
00:14:01.052 --> 00:14:17.393
Candidate retrieval from the search index (OpenSearch or Elasticsearch-style): geo filter: properties inside the polygon or map bounding box;. static filters: property type, amenities, stars;. result: ~3,000 candidates.

241
00:14:17.673 --> 00:14:20.703
Availability and price (§5.3).

242
00:14:22.053 --> 00:14:39.226
For each candidate, the search service asks the in-memory availability or price cache, sharded by property: is there a room for 2 adults for each night 29, 30, 31 Dec, satisfying min stay and closed-to-arrival rules, and what is the cheapest total price?

243
00:14:39.506 --> 00:14:46.077
The cache keeps per-property, per-date compact arrays, so each check takes microseconds (§6.1).

244
00:14:46.357 --> 00:14:49.343
About 1,200 properties are available.

245
00:14:50.693 --> 00:14:51.525
Pricing.

246
00:14:51.805 --> 00:15:07.507
The pricing service applies taxes (GST by tariff slab; VERIFY), platform fees, member discounts, coupons where eligible, and currency conversion, giving a display price that includes taxes as regulations and UX require.

247
00:15:07.787 --> 00:15:09.685
Ranking (§6.3).

248
00:15:09.965 --> 00:15:26.349
The ranking service scores the 1,200 properties with features such as quality, conversion history, price competitiveness, distance to the area centre, review score, Anita's past preferences (for example, she books boutique stays), and listing embeddings.

249
00:15:27.699 --> 00:15:34.334
Business rules apply: sponsored placements are labelled, and diversity rules keep one brand from dominating.

250
00:15:34.614 --> 00:15:35.531
Response.

251
00:15:35.811 --> 00:15:41.401
The top 30 results go back with prices and badges (Free cancellation, Only 2 left).

252
00:15:41.681 --> 00:15:44.646
The map view loads pins for the visible bounding box.

253
00:15:44.926 --> 00:15:45.715
Logging.

254
00:15:45.995 --> 00:15:52.587
The impressions (what was shown, in which position) are logged to Kafka for ranking model training and experiments.

255
00:15:53.937 --> 00:15:56.007
Journey 3: booking a hotel room.

256
00:15:56.287 --> 00:15:57.375
Room selection.

257
00:15:57.655 --> 00:15:59.553
Anita opens a property page.

258
00:15:59.833 --> 00:16:05.423
The service fetches detailed rates for the dates: all room types and rate plans, with policies.

259
00:16:05.703 --> 00:16:17.095
For some partners the page does a live availability call to the channel manager or supplier API to get exact prices (§6.6), because cache staleness matters.

260
00:16:17.375 --> 00:16:26.505
She picks Deluxe Sea View, breakfast included, free cancellation until 26 Dec at 54,000 rupees + taxes for 3 nights.

261
00:16:26.785 --> 00:16:28.044
Booking initiation.

262
00:16:28.324 --> 00:16:29.497
The booking service:

263
00:16:30.847 --> 00:16:53.759
re-prices exactly (price mismatch check: if the price has changed, it shows the new price and asks Anita to accept);. places a hold on inventory, decrementing the allotment atomically in the ARI store for each night (§5.4), or creates a pending reservation with the partner for live-connected hotels;. runs fraud checks (§6.7).

264
00:16:54.039 --> 00:16:54.829
Payment.

265
00:16:55.109 --> 00:16:57.349
Anita chooses pay now by UPI.

266
00:16:57.629 --> 00:17:01.682
Payment is processed with an idempotency key (Ch 45).

267
00:17:03.032 --> 00:17:05.315
On success the booking moves to CONFIRMED.

268
00:17:05.595 --> 00:17:12.443
Or she picks pay at hotel: a card guarantee may be required, or no payment for trusted users or partners.

269
00:17:12.723 --> 00:17:14.067
Delivery to the hotel.

270
00:17:14.347 --> 00:17:21.920
The booking is sent to the channel manager or PMS via the connectivity gateway (OTAHotelResNotifRQ).

271
00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.933
The hotel's system acknowledges with its own confirmation number.

272
00:17:27.283 --> 00:17:29.843
If delivery fails, it retries with alerts.

273
00:17:30.123 --> 00:17:34.561
Undelivered bookings are critical: the guest could arrive with no reservation.

274
00:17:34.841 --> 00:17:35.865
Confirmation.

275
00:17:36.145 --> 00:17:43.163
Anita gets an email, SMS and app voucher with the hotel's confirmation number and the cancellation policy.

276
00:17:43.443 --> 00:17:45.811
The invoice includes GST details.

277
00:17:46.091 --> 00:17:47.137
After booking.

278
00:17:47.417 --> 00:17:53.283
Reminders, pre-check-in details (ID upload, arrival time), and messaging with the hotel.

279
00:17:54.633 --> 00:17:57.449
Journey 4: booking a homestay with request-to-book.

280
00:17:57.729 --> 00:17:58.497
Search.

281
00:17:58.777 --> 00:18:01.316
Rahul finds a villa for 6 guests in Coorg.

282
00:18:01.596 --> 00:18:03.559
The host requires request-to-book.

283
00:18:03.839 --> 00:18:04.713
Request.

284
00:18:04.993 --> 00:18:08.769
Rahul sends a request with a message about trip purpose and guests.

285
00:18:09.049 --> 00:18:17.967
The platform pre-authorises his payment method, holding the amount where supported, or collects payment that will be refunded if the request is declined.

286
00:18:18.247 --> 00:18:22.791
The calendar dates are tentatively blocked for the response window (24 h).

287
00:18:24.141 --> 00:18:29.005
The host sees Rahul's profile (verification status, past reviews) and accepts.

288
00:18:29.285 --> 00:18:32.122
The booking is confirmed and the payment is captured.

289
00:18:32.402 --> 00:18:33.426
Calendar sync.

290
00:18:33.706 --> 00:18:38.058
The dates are blocked on the platform calendar, and the iCal export updates.

291
00:18:38.338 --> 00:18:46.807
Other sites the host uses import the iCal and block the dates within their polling interval, which can take hours (§6.5).

292
00:18:47.087 --> 00:18:47.919
Payout.

293
00:18:48.199 --> 00:18:57.970
The host is paid 24 hours after check-in (publicly described practice for some marketplaces; VERIFY), minus the host fee, through bank transfer.

294
00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:01.514
Guests are protected if the listing isn't as described.

295
00:19:02.864 --> 00:19:03.696
Reviews.

296
00:19:03.976 --> 00:19:07.219
After checkout both sides have 14 days to review.

297
00:19:07.499 --> 00:19:12.235
Reviews are revealed together or at the deadline, so neither side retaliates.

298
00:19:13.585 --> 00:19:15.782
Journey 5: overbooking at check-in.

299
00:19:16.062 --> 00:19:16.958
The cause.

300
00:19:17.238 --> 00:19:22.465
A hotel sells its last room on two channels within a minute, before channel sync completes.

301
00:19:22.745 --> 00:19:24.323
Both bookings are confirmed.

302
00:19:24.603 --> 00:19:25.521
Detection.

303
00:19:25.801 --> 00:19:32.819
The hotel's PMS flags the overbooking, and the hotel tells the OTA (or the guest arrives and there's no room).

304
00:19:33.099 --> 00:19:34.550
Relocation policy.

305
00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:43.534
The OTA's support system finds a comparable or better property nearby at the same price, and the OTA or the hotel pays the difference.

306
00:19:44.884 --> 00:19:50.516
It arranges transport and notifies the guest proactively if the problem is known in advance.

307
00:19:50.796 --> 00:19:51.884
Accountability.

308
00:19:52.164 --> 00:19:55.321
The OTA records the incident against the hotel.

309
00:19:55.601 --> 00:19:59.164
Repeated overbookings affect ranking and lead to penalties.

310
00:19:59.444 --> 00:20:00.340
Prevention.

311
00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:02.092
Faster ARI sync.

312
00:20:02.372 --> 00:20:07.044
Allotment buffers (sell only Nminus 1 of the last rooms on some channels).

313
00:20:07.324 --> 00:20:10.652
Live availability checks at booking for high-demand dates.

314
00:20:12.002 --> 00:20:14.413
Journey 6: cancellation and refund.

315
00:20:14.693 --> 00:20:15.567
Request.

316
00:20:15.847 --> 00:20:17.682
Anita cancels on 20 Dec.

317
00:20:17.962 --> 00:20:23.402
The rate plan allowed free cancellation until 26 Dec, so she gets a full refund.

318
00:20:23.682 --> 00:20:37.613
The booking service: applies the policy;. computes the refund (minus any non-refundable fees, per policy and regulations);. sends a cancellation to the hotel (OTACancelRQ) and gets an acknowledgement;.

319
00:20:38.963 --> 00:20:52.445
releases inventory (re-increments the allotment), or the hotel's next ARI update reflects it;. triggers the refund through the payment service (UPI refunds take minutes to days; VERIFY timelines).

320
00:20:52.725 --> 00:20:54.133
Non-refundable rates.

321
00:20:54.413 --> 00:20:59.683
No refund, though the platform may help with exceptions (illness, disasters) per policy.

322
00:20:59.963 --> 00:21:00.880
Homestays.

323
00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:06.109
Policies are set by the host from platform templates (flexible, moderate, strict).

324
00:21:06.389 --> 00:21:12.427
Extenuating circumstances policies cover disasters (VERIFY specific platform policies).

325
00:21:13.777 --> 00:21:14.737
Part 5.

326
00:21:15.017 --> 00:21:16.553
Core Subsystems in Depth.

327
00:21:17.803 --> 00:21:19.232
ARI data model.

328
00:21:19.512 --> 00:21:41.421
Entities: property, then room types (Deluxe, Suite), each with max occupancy, beds and physical inventory;. rate plans per room type (Room only, Breakfast, Non-refundable, Member rate, Long stay), each with a cancellation policy, meal plan, occupancy-based prices and derived rules (for example, member rate = base minus 10%).

329
00:21:41.701 --> 00:21:47.717
Per date per room type: inventory (rooms available to sell), sold count, and a stop-sell flag.

330
00:21:49.067 --> 00:22:03.979
Per date per rate plan: price by occupancy (1 adult, 2 adults, extra adult or child);. restrictions: min or max length of stay, closed to arrival (CTA), closed to departure (CTD), advance purchase windows.

331
00:22:04.259 --> 00:22:05.369
Derived rates.

332
00:22:05.649 --> 00:22:12.049
Some rate plans derive from a parent (Breakfast = Room only + 800 rupees or person).

333
00:22:12.329 --> 00:22:17.321
They are stored as rules and computed at read time or materialised in the cache.

334
00:22:17.601 --> 00:22:18.475
Storage.

335
00:22:19.825 --> 00:22:29.575
A wide-column or key-value store keyed by (property, room type, rate plan) with date-indexed arrays or bitmaps for the horizon (§6.1).

336
00:22:29.855 --> 00:22:33.887
Or a relational table partitioned by property, with a row per date.

337
00:22:34.167 --> 00:22:36.940
That is simpler, but heavier at 16B cells.

338
00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:39.442
Content service.

339
00:22:39.722 --> 00:22:46.485
Property details, room types and photos, amenities (taxonomy), policies, location and translations.

340
00:22:46.765 --> 00:22:48.194
Hosts edit through the app.

341
00:22:48.474 --> 00:22:51.845
Hotels update through the extranet or content APIs.

342
00:22:52.125 --> 00:22:59.997
Photo pipeline: upload, then resize and compress, then quality and duplicate checks, then a CDN (Ch 52).

343
00:23:00.277 --> 00:23:05.482
Quality scoring: photo count and quality, description completeness, amenity accuracy.

344
00:23:05.762 --> 00:23:06.957
This feeds ranking.

345
00:23:08.307 --> 00:23:10.077
Search: two-stage retrieval.

346
00:23:10.357 --> 00:23:24.245
Stage 1: candidate retrieval from an inverted plus geo index: geo (geohash or BKD tree for bounding boxes, polygons, distance);. attributes (type, stars, amenities);. text (name, area).

347
00:23:24.525 --> 00:23:29.240
The index updates when content changes, which is rare compared with ARI.

348
00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:31.909
Stage 2: availability and pricing.

349
00:23:33.259 --> 00:23:45.270
An in-memory cache sharded by property ID holds, per property, compact per-date structures: availability count per room type, the lowest price per occupancy per date, and restriction flags.

350
00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:55.321
The search service fans out to the shards for its candidates (scatter, gather) and gets back available properties with a lead price (cheapest total for the stay).

351
00:23:55.601 --> 00:23:58.011
Stage 3: ranking and pagination.

352
00:23:58.291 --> 00:24:00.361
Score, sort and return the top N.

353
00:24:00.641 --> 00:24:07.617
Cache whole query results briefly (for example, 1 to 5 minutes) for popular city + date combinations.

354
00:24:08.967 --> 00:24:09.905
Map search.

355
00:24:10.185 --> 00:24:12.575
Re-query on map pan with a bounding box.

356
00:24:12.855 --> 00:24:14.348
Cluster pins at low zoom.

357
00:24:15.698 --> 00:24:17.789
Booking service and inventory holds.

358
00:24:18.069 --> 00:24:19.093
State machine:

359
00:24:19.373 --> 00:24:26.882
INITIATED, then HELD, then PAYMENTPENDING, then CONFIRMED, then (MODIFIED), then CANCELLED or CHECKEDIN, then COMPLETED.

360
00:24:27.162 --> 00:24:29.466
Failure paths go to EXPIRED or FAILED.

361
00:24:29.746 --> 00:24:30.493
Hold.

362
00:24:30.773 --> 00:24:42.250
An atomic conditional decrement per night: if inventory minus sold ≥ rooms then sold += rooms, all nights in one transaction for the property partition.

363
00:24:42.530 --> 00:24:49.399
Or a reservation record with a TTL (for example, 15 minutes) that the cache counts as unavailable.

364
00:24:50.749 --> 00:24:53.160
Expired holds are released by a sweeper.

365
00:24:53.440 --> 00:24:54.357
Homestays.

366
00:24:54.637 --> 00:25:01.571
The calendar is a single unit, so a conditional write on all dates is enough: block the dates only if they are all free.

367
00:25:01.851 --> 00:25:06.544
Use optimistic concurrency (a version on the calendar) or a lock per listing.

368
00:25:06.824 --> 00:25:08.317
Live-connected hotels.

369
00:25:08.597 --> 00:25:10.624
Call the supplier's booking API.

370
00:25:10.904 --> 00:25:12.696
The response decides success.

371
00:25:12.976 --> 00:25:18.053
On timeout, query the status before retrying, to avoid duplicate reservations.

372
00:25:18.333 --> 00:25:22.600
Idempotency on client requests, payment callbacks and supplier calls.

373
00:25:23.950 --> 00:25:25.315
Channel connectivity.

374
00:25:25.595 --> 00:25:28.411
Inbound ARI: push from channel managers.

375
00:25:28.691 --> 00:25:31.934
There are thousands of partners with varied reliability.

376
00:25:32.214 --> 00:25:34.326
Use queues and per-partner rate limits.

377
00:25:34.606 --> 00:25:43.011
Outbound bookings: reservations, modifications and cancellations, with retries, acknowledgements and a dead-letter queue with alerts.

378
00:25:43.291 --> 00:25:48.113
Mapping: the OTA's room and rate IDs ↔ the partner's IDs.

379
00:25:48.393 --> 00:25:53.491
Mapping errors cause wrong prices, so validate with rules and alert on anomalies.

380
00:25:53.771 --> 00:25:57.206
Rate parity monitoring: compare prices across channels.

381
00:25:57.486 --> 00:26:04.462
Parity clauses are subject to competition law in some jurisdictions (VERIFY CCI rulings in India).

382
00:26:05.812 --> 00:26:07.668
Payments, payouts and commission.

383
00:26:07.948 --> 00:26:15.073
Merchant model: the OTA charges the guest, pays the hotel net of commission on a cycle, and issues invoices.

384
00:26:15.353 --> 00:26:18.020
Agency model: the guest pays the hotel.

385
00:26:18.300 --> 00:26:21.436
The OTA invoices the hotel for commission monthly.

386
00:26:21.716 --> 00:26:25.428
Pay-at-hotel no-shows need card guarantees or policies.

387
00:26:25.708 --> 00:26:26.625
Homestays:

388
00:26:26.905 --> 00:26:28.868
The platform collects the full amount.

389
00:26:29.148 --> 00:26:32.455
Funds are held until check-in, then the payout is released.

390
00:26:33.805 --> 00:26:36.557
Refunds are handled with policy and guarantees.

391
00:26:36.837 --> 00:26:43.471
A double-entry ledger tracks guest payments, fees, host payables and refunds (I03, I11).

392
00:26:43.751 --> 00:26:44.669
Taxes:

393
00:26:44.949 --> 00:26:53.418
GST on the room tariff and on platform services; TCS or TDS obligations for e-commerce operators (VERIFY).

394
00:26:54.768 --> 00:26:56.005
Reviews and trust.

395
00:26:56.285 --> 00:26:57.821
Verified stays only.

396
00:26:58.101 --> 00:27:00.320
Reviews are linked to completed bookings.

397
00:27:00.600 --> 00:27:09.837
Ratings: sub-ratings (cleanliness, location, value, communication), aggregated with Bayesian averaging so a few reviews don't dominate.

398
00:27:10.117 --> 00:27:12.955
Fake review detection (§6.8).

399
00:27:13.235 --> 00:27:19.912
Safety: identity verification for hosts and guests, reporting, and a 24 or 7 safety line.

400
00:27:20.192 --> 00:27:26.720
Listing quality: duplicate listing detection, and fake or scam listings (for example, stolen photos).

401
00:27:28.070 --> 00:27:29.009
Part 6.

402
00:27:29.289 --> 00:27:30.249
Algorithms.

403
00:27:31.499 --> 00:27:34.464
Calendar representation and date-range queries.

404
00:27:34.744 --> 00:27:41.507
Per room type: an array indexed by day offset from today, holding available counts (16-bit integers).

405
00:27:41.787 --> 00:27:45.392
A 500-day horizon is 1 KB per room type.

406
00:27:45.672 --> 00:28:02.355
Stay check: for check-in day d and N nights, require min(availabled... d+Nminus 1) ≥ rooms;. also check the rate plan restrictions: min stay at arrival date at most N, no CTA on d, no CTD on d+N.

407
00:28:03.705 --> 00:28:05.731
N is small, so a scan is fast.

408
00:28:06.011 --> 00:28:15.163
For long stays or flexible-date searches, sparse tables or segment trees answer range-min queries in O(1)/O(log n).

409
00:28:15.443 --> 00:28:17.555
Homestays: a bitmap of booked days.

410
00:28:17.835 --> 00:28:23.467
The stay is available if (bitmap AND maskd... d+Nminus 1) == 0.

411
00:28:23.747 --> 00:28:26.393
This is a word-level AND, and extremely fast.

412
00:28:26.673 --> 00:28:35.355
Price for a stay: the sum over nights of the price for that occupancy, plus extra-guest charges, and length-of-stay discounts (weekly, monthly).

413
00:28:35.635 --> 00:28:38.963
Precompute prefix sums per rate plan for quick totals.

414
00:28:40.313 --> 00:28:46.159
Flexible dates (weekend in March): evaluate a few candidate windows with the same structures.

415
00:28:47.509 --> 00:28:48.575
Geo search.

416
00:28:48.855 --> 00:28:56.109
Index: a geohash or BKD tree (Lucene geo points) for bounding box, polygon and distance queries.

417
00:28:56.389 --> 00:29:03.685
Ranking distance: distance to the searched landmark or area centroid, or distance to popular points learned from bookings.

418
00:29:03.965 --> 00:29:09.703
Area boundaries: neighbourhood polygons are curated, or learned from where people search and book.

419
00:29:11.053 --> 00:29:12.760
Ranking: learning to rank.

420
00:29:13.040 --> 00:29:19.525
Objective: maximise bookings (and guest satisfaction) per search, with the result position bias modelled.

421
00:29:19.805 --> 00:29:39.027
Features: listing: price relative to the area's typical price, review score and count, photo quality, cancellation policy, host response rate, past CTR or CVR;. query: destination, dates, guests, lead time, length of stay;. user: past bookings, price sensitivity, preferred property types;.

422
00:29:40.377 --> 00:29:42.254
context: device, locale.

423
00:29:42.534 --> 00:29:43.323
Models:

424
00:29:43.603 --> 00:29:49.619
Gradient-boosted trees (LambdaMART) for pairwise or listwise ranking, then deep neural networks.

425
00:29:49.899 --> 00:30:10.401
Airbnb publicly described moving from GBDT to neural networks, and using listing embeddings learned from click sessions (word2vec-style, where listings are words and sessions are sentences) for similar-listing and real-time personalisation (KDD 2018 or 2019 papers; VERIFY).

426
00:30:11.751 --> 00:30:25.532
Training data: impressions with clicks and bookings;. correction for position bias (inverse propensity weighting, or randomised exploration);. booked listings as positives, with clicked-but-not-booked as weaker signals.

427
00:30:25.812 --> 00:30:27.241
Online evaluation:

428
00:30:27.521 --> 00:30:33.580
A or B tests on conversion and revenue, with guardrails on cancellations and guest satisfaction.

429
00:30:33.860 --> 00:30:38.703
Booking.com publicly emphasises large-scale experimentation (VERIFY).

430
00:30:40.053 --> 00:30:51.189
Business layer: sponsored listings (labelled), diversity, fairness to new listings (a cold-start boost with exploration), and demotion for poor quality or high cancellations.

431
00:30:52.539 --> 00:30:54.992
Dynamic pricing and revenue management.

432
00:30:55.272 --> 00:31:16.093
Hotels (classic revenue management): forecast demand per date from booking pace (bookings on the books versus the same time last year), events and seasonality;. set prices to maximise RevPAR (revenue per available room);. length-of-stay controls (min stay at peak), and overbooking levels (§6.6).

433
00:31:16.373 --> 00:31:18.741
This often runs in the hotel's RMS.

434
00:31:19.021 --> 00:31:21.176
The OTA provides market insights.

435
00:31:22.526 --> 00:31:35.497
Homestay price suggestions (publicly described as Smart Pricing by Airbnb; VERIFY): predict the booking probability at different prices for each night, from listing features, seasonality, lead time,

436
00:31:35.777 --> 00:31:49.707
local demand (searches for those dates) and competitor prices;. pick the price that maximises expected revenue within the host's min or max;. price elasticity is estimated from historical data and experiments.

437
00:31:51.057 --> 00:31:56.647
Platform discounts: member prices and coupons, with budget control (Ch 49).

438
00:31:57.997 --> 00:32:05.954
Calendar sync and double-booking prevention. iCal sync: hosts listing on multiple sites export and import iCal feeds.

439
00:32:06.234 --> 00:32:09.754
Polling intervals (often hours) create double-booking windows.

440
00:32:10.034 --> 00:32:13.277
Mitigations: more frequent polling for active listings;.

441
00:32:13.557 --> 00:32:20.063
API-based channel sync (real-time) where available;. a buffer (block same-day bookings until synced);.

442
00:32:21.413 --> 00:32:30.800
conflict detection: when an imported event overlaps an existing booking, alert the host immediately and run the cancellation or rebooking workflow.

443
00:32:32.150 --> 00:32:34.027
Overbooking control (hotels).

444
00:32:34.307 --> 00:32:43.481
Why hotels overbook: cancellations and no-shows leave rooms empty, so they sell beyond capacity by an amount based on expected no-shows.

445
00:32:43.761 --> 00:32:48.454
The model: choose the overbooking level k to maximise expected revenue.

446
00:32:48.734 --> 00:32:54.558
The revenue from extra bookings is weighed against the cost of walking a guest (relocation, goodwill).

447
00:32:54.838 --> 00:33:02.433
Use no-show and cancellation distributions by date, segment and rate plan (non-refundable rates have fewer no-shows).

448
00:33:02.713 --> 00:33:12.590
Classic approach: a newsvendor-style calculation: overbook while P(show-ups capacity) times walk cost the expected revenue of the extra room.

449
00:33:13.940 --> 00:33:23.007
OTA role: respect the hotel's overbooking settings, keep extra-channel buffers on scarce inventory, and run live checks for the last rooms.

450
00:33:24.357 --> 00:33:25.445
Fraud detection.

451
00:33:25.725 --> 00:33:31.869
Payment fraud: stolen cards booking high-value stays (often last-minute bookings in popular cities).

452
00:33:32.149 --> 00:33:34.602
Account takeover: loyalty points theft.

453
00:33:34.882 --> 00:33:39.917
Host scams: fake listings, or off-platform payment requests (pay me directly).

454
00:33:40.197 --> 00:33:43.717
Signals: device and IP reputation;. velocity;.

455
00:33:45.067 --> 00:33:58.272
the mismatch between card country, IP and destination;. lead time and booking value;. new accounts;. message text classifiers that detect requests for off-platform payment or contact details.

456
00:33:58.552 --> 00:34:06.616
Actions: step-up authentication (3DS, ID verification), holds, cancellation and refund, and listing takedown.

457
00:34:07.966 --> 00:34:09.993
Review integrity and aggregation.

458
00:34:10.273 --> 00:34:19.169
Bayesian average: score = (C times m + Σ ratings) / (C + n), where m is the prior mean and C the prior weight.

459
00:34:19.449 --> 00:34:22.670
This avoids a single 5-star review ranking at the top.

460
00:34:22.950 --> 00:34:34.129
Fake review detection: text similarity across reviews;. reviewer graphs (rings of accounts reviewing each other);. bursts of reviews;. review sentiment versus ratings mismatch;.

461
00:34:35.479 --> 00:34:37.079
verified-stay requirement.

462
00:34:37.359 --> 00:34:43.183
Review summarisation: aspect-based sentiment (cleanliness, staff, location) shown as highlights.

463
00:34:43.463 --> 00:34:46.769
LLM-based summaries with grounding to actual reviews.

464
00:34:48.119 --> 00:34:49.869
Duplicate property detection.

465
00:34:50.149 --> 00:34:57.573
The problem: the same hotel arrives via multiple suppliers or channel managers, and the same home is listed twice.

466
00:34:57.853 --> 00:35:08.242
Matching: name similarity (fuzzy match, transliteration);. address normalisation;. geo distance;. phone and website matches;. photo perceptual hashes.

467
00:35:09.592 --> 00:35:18.701
Resolution: merge into one canonical property with multiple supply sources (for an aggregator OTA), or flag the duplicate listing.

